-- title:
--   Nonvanishing of some Lange–Ruppert chart element for j=1
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a Noetherian integral domain, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ satisfying `W.IsElliptic`. For an index $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, write $\mathcal A_i$ for the homogeneous localisation `HomogeneousLocalization.Away` of the graded ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,3, R)/(F)$ — the quotient of the polynomial ring in three variables by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic $F$ attached to `W.toProjective`, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules — at the image of the variable $X_i$; each $\mathcal A_i$ is an $R$-algebra through the composite of $R \to (\text{degree-}0\text{ part})$ with the map to the localisation. The family `kw_lrSixU W i 1`, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,3 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, consists of the six elements of $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_1$ obtained by evaluating, on the chart pair $(i,1)$, the three coordinates of the Lange–Ruppert addition vector (on the left summand) and of its symmetrised counterpart (on the right summand). The theorem asserts that there exists an index $l$ with `kw_lrSixU W i 1 l` $\neq 0$ in $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_1$.
--
--   The statement records that, with the right chart fixed to the $Y$-chart $j = 1$, the six dehomogenised Lange–Ruppert addition-law elements do not all vanish on the tensor chart $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_1$; this nonvanishing is what allows the addition law to be used to define a morphism on that chart. It is the $j = 1$ case feeding into [`WeierstrassProjModel.exists_lrSixU_ne_zero_of_isElliptic`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.exists_lrSixU_ne_zero_of_isElliptic), where the general pair of charts is treated.
